  "resources": ["SageMaker Model Registry model package groups and model packages in us-east-1"],
  "timeframe": "Last 90 days (CloudTrail lookup supports up to 90 days) - 2026-08-16T00:00:00Z to 2026-11-14T04:42:10Z",
  "criteria": "1) List model package groups and, per group, the count of model package versions by ModelApprovalStatus (Approved / PendingManualApproval / Rejected). For approved versions, note ApprovalDescription and LastModifiedBy / CreatedBy where available. 2) Use CloudTrail (lookup_cloudtrail_events) for sagemaker UpdateModelPackage and CreateModelPackage events (look at requestParameters.modelApprovalStatus) to determine WHO set Approved: human IAM/SSO users vs. service roles (CodePipeline, Lambda, Step Functions, SageMaker Pipelines execution role, EventBridge-triggered automation) and whether CreateModelPackage was called with ModelApprovalStatus=Approved directly (auto-approved at registration). Compute time gap between creation and approval per version when possible. 3) Check for any automation that could auto-approve: SageMaker Pipelines RegisterModel/ModelStep steps with approval_status='Approved', EventBridge rules on 'SageMaker Model Package State Change', Lambda functions that call update_model_package, and any IAM/approval gating config visible. Do not change permissions. 4) Give a clear verdict (manual vs auto-approved vs mixed), with numbers per group, example event identities and timestamps, and caveats (e.g. events older than 90 days not visible, other regions/accounts not checked)."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit SageMaker Model Registry approvals in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

